  "label": "Stephen Hawking in wheelchair with overlaid text implying he was a donor for go-cart parts",
  "description": "The scene depicts Stephen Hawking seated in his wheelchair, with overlaid text that reads 'does anyone know if he had a donor card?' and 'i need parts for my go-cart.' The juxtaposition of Hawking's physical condition with the absurd, disrespectful implication that he might have been a source of spare parts for a go-cart creates a darkly comedic effect. The scene is structured to highlight the visual contrast between Hawking's dignified presence and the crude, insensitive joke, which is the core of the meme's intent.",
